ementation, managed service, integration, and proof of concept projects.","Need dashboards for project health, progress, overdue tasks, blockers, upcoming milestones, risks, resource load, active projects, project value, resource utilization, and customer issues.","Need auditability for approvals, including who approved, when, and comments.","Need role-based and project-based permissions because operations are matrix-based.","Need careful handling of sensitive data such as pricing, margin, contracts, customer data, and technical credentials.","Need adoption-friendly workflows because many users still feel chat is sufficient and will resist systems with too many steps."],"decision_agreement":["PT Prasetia Dwidharma will evaluate Lark Suite through a limited pilot rather than a full tool replacement.","Core proposed pilot areas are sales-to-project handover and project tracking.","Resource request approval is a strong candidate for the pilot but remains subject to validation with the resource manager.","AI meeting summary will be treated as a supporting feature, not a separate pilot workstream.","The first pilot should be internal only, without customer guest access.","Pilot participant estimate is 40 to 60 users, with approximately 20 to 30 core users and the rest as approvers or stakeholders.","Pilot duration under consideration is six to eight weeks.","Security, API, SSO, AI data handling, and integrations will be handled in a separate technical session with IT.","Full offline capability will not be assumed or committed before technical validation.","Email migration, payroll, core finance, secret management, full historical document migration, and full resource capacity planning are out of scope for the pilot."],"action_items":["PT Prasetia Dwidharma: Kodrat Santoso to send sanitized examples of current handover templates and weekly project reports within three working days.","PT Prasetia Dwidharma: Kodrat Santoso to propose business workshop participants, targeted