upport for meeting summaries, decisions, action items, and search, with user review and security controls."],"key_discussions":["Current collaboration landscape and impact of fragmented tools on handover, reporting, approvals, and knowledge management.","Potential pilot scope covering structured handover, project tracking, resource request approval, and AI meeting summary.","Success metrics including report preparation time, meeting minutes effort, handover completeness, overdue visibility, adoption, approval turnaround time, and clarification after kickoff.","Technical and security topics including API, webhook, SSO, audit log, data residency, retention, DLP, AI data processing, permissions, guest access, and offline limitations.","Pilot planning, stakeholder involvement, workshop structure, prototype expectations, training, support, and internal risks."],"decisions_agreements":["PT Prasetia Dwidharma will evaluate Lark Suite through a limited pilot approach rather than replacing all existing tools immediately.","Core proposed pilot scope is sales-to-project handover and project tracking, while resource request approval remains a strong candidate subject to validation with the resource manager.","AI meeting summary will be treated as a supporting feature with user review before creating tasks or updating records.","Initial pilot will be internal only, without direct customer guest access.","Business use case\\/prototype workshop and a separate technical workshop for security, API, SSO, and integration will be planned."]},"meeting_type_sections":{"discovery_objectives":["Understand PT Prasetia Dwidharma's current collaboration, project management, approval, and knowledge management workflows.","Identify priority use cases where Lark Suite could deliver measurable operational value.","Define a realistic pilot scope and success metrics without overextending into full tool replacement."],"current_state":{"communication":"Fast communication primarily uses WhatsApp; formal communication uses email.","documents":"Documents are stored in Google Drive and sometimes OneDrive depending on division.","task_tracking":"Tracking uses spreadsheets and some task management applications, but usage is not standardized.","approvals":"Approvals are handled through email, chat, forms, and manual processes.","reporting":"Weekly project reporting is manually consolidated from multiple files with inconsistent formats."},"business_challenges":["No consistent single source of truth across sales, presales, project, finance, procurement, and support.","Project kickoff can be delayed because handover documents are incomplete or inconsistent.","Delivery teams may interpret scope differently from sales discussions due to separated information sources.","Management dashboards require significant manual work to appear complete and organized.","Users often depend on individuals to locate historical information, decisions, or context."],"priority_use_cases":[{"use_case":"Sales-to-Project Handover","priority":"High","description":"Sales submits structured handover data, presales confirms technical scope, project manager accepts or returns incomplete handover, and accepted handover can create a project workspace or project record."},{"use_case":"Project Tracking","priority":"High","description":"Track milestones, tasks, owners, due dates, status, risks, issues, weekly updates, overdue items, blockers, upcoming milestones, and project health."},{"use_case":"Resource Request Approval","priority":"Medium-High","description":"Project managers request roles, skills, headcount, period, location, allocation, and urgency; approval routing is defined while availability is manually verified during pilot."},{"use_case":"AI Meeting Summary","priority":"Medium","description":"Generate meeting summaries, decisions, pain points, action items, PIC, due dates, and recommendations, subject to user review before system updates."}],"pilot_scope":{"proposed_in_scope":["Structured sales-to-project handover","Project tracking with dashboard","Resource request approval, subject to validation with resource manager","AI meeting summary as supporting feature","Mobile approval and mobile task update demonstration","Internal pilot users only"],"out_of_scope":["Payroll","Core finance replacement","Customer credential management or secret management","Full historical document migration","Full resource capacity planning","Email migration","Full offline commitment before technical validation"],"estimated_users":"Approximately 40-60 pilot users, with 20-30 core users and the rest approvers or stakeholders.","pilot_duration":"Minimum 6 weeks; 8 weeks may be ideal depending on effort and cost."},"success_metrics":["Reduction in weekly project report preparation time.","Reduction in meeting minutes administration time.","Improvement in handover completeness.","Visibility of overdue actions, blockers, and milestones.","User adoption and reduction of fallback to old tools.","Approval turnaround time.","Percentage of required handover fields completed.","Number of handovers returned for completion.","Time from closed-won to project accepted.","Number of clarification requests after kickoff."],"stakeholders_identified":[{"name":"Kodrat Santoso","role":"Project Manager, evaluator, use-case project owner, potential champion","organization":"PT Prasetia Dwidharma"},{"name":"Head of IT","role":"Likely final decision support and technical\\/security stakeholder","organization":"PT Prasetia Dwidharma"},{"name":"Director terkait","role":"Likely final decision maker","organization":"PT Prasetia Dwidharma"},{"name":"Finance and Procurement","role":"Commercial evaluation, procurement, vendor registration, finance-related approvals","organization":"PT Prasetia Dwidharma"},{"name":"Resource Manager","role":"Needed to validate resource request workflow","organization":"PT Prasetia Dwidharma"}],"technical_requirements":["Conditional approval routing by nominal value, department, project, document type, and transaction conditions.","Audit trail for approvals showing who approved, when, and comments.","Project templates by category such as implementation, managed service, integration, and proof of concept.","Configurable task dependencies with a balance between governance and flexibility.","Permission model supporting department and matrix project structures.","API, webhook, bot, and integration capability for Base, Approval, Messenger, Calendar, and Documents.","Mobile support for approval, chat, project status, task updates, forms, photo uploads, site name, timestamp, and notes."],"security_compliance_considerations":["SSO is important for long-term rollout.","Audit log is important.","Data residency, retention, and DLP require input from IT\\/security.","External collaboration is interesting but requires strict guest access control, folder\\/document permissions, and easy access revocation.","Search must follow source permissions, especially for conversations and sensitive content.","AI data processing location, storage, provider access, and controls must be clarified before using sensitive customer meeting data.","Credential management should remain in a secret manager, not regular collaboration documents."],"integrations":{"phase_1":"Integrations should be limited to avoid slowing pilot; not all integrations are required initially.","future_or_later_phase":["Email","Calendar","Internal CRM","Project system","ERP","Automation tools","Custom API or webhook integrations"],"not_replacing":"Lark should not replace the ERP or core financial system; it may display operational summaries or billing status in later phases."},"risks_constraints":["No approved budget yet.","Final decision makers and IT\\/security stakeholders were not present in this discovery meeting.","User resistance to change, especially from users who believe chat is sufficient.","Availability of users for workshops may be limited due to ongoing major projects.","Initial data and templates are not fully clean or standardized.","Offline capability must be technically validated and should not be overpromised.","AI capabilities must be governed and reviewed by users, not treated as automatically authoritative."],"missing_information":["Approved budget or budget range.","Names of Head of IT, infrastructure PIC, director decision maker, finance approver, and resource manager.","Detailed security requirements for data residency, retention, SSO configuration, audit log scope, DLP, and AI data processing.","Exact current templates for handover and weekly project report.","Final pilot scope confirmation after business workshop and resource manager validation.","Formal procurement timeline and vendor registration requirements.","Exact baseline metrics before pilot measurement starts."]},"detailed_insights":{"topics_discussed":[{"topik":"Current collaboration fragmentation","ringkasan":"The customer uses WhatsApp, email, Google Drive, OneDrive, spreadsheets, task tools, and manual forms inconsistently across divisions and processes.","relevansi":"High"},{"topik":"Sales-to-project handover","ringkasan":"Handover suffers from missing data, inconsistent naming, different proposal versions, and critical decisions stored only in chat, causing kickoff delay and scope misunderstanding.","relevansi":"High"},{"topik":"Project tracking and dashboards","ringkasan":"The customer manages around 20-30 active projects on average, with more when including small projects, proof of concepts, and support; management needs project health, risks, overdue tasks, milestones, resource load, and issue visibility.","relevansi":"High"},{"topik":"Approval workflow","ringkasan":"Resource request, procurement, business trip, reimbursement, and commercial document approvals require conditional routing, audit trail, and mobile access.","relevansi":"High"},{"topik":"Knowledge management and document control","ringkasan":"Old project documents, lesson learned, proposal examples, t