66	App\\Models\\LeadTranscript	23	meeting_summary_generation	{"meeting_type":"Demo","summary_type":"Demo","general_sections":{"executive_summary":"PT TPLink Indonesia (Technology & IT Services) attended a demo of Lark, an all-in-one collaboration platform by ByteDance, presented by Prasetya (a platinum partner). The meeting covered Lark's core features: Messenger, Calendar, Meetings with real-time translation, Lark Base (a powerful database and project management tool), Approval workflows, and internal social media. The customer, currently using WhatsApp and multiple separate apps, expressed strong interest in Lark Base and Approval features to automate processes and improve collaboration. Key discussions included pricing (Lark Pro vs Enterprise for 80 users), implementation timeline, training and adoption phases, server location (Singapore\\/Japan), SLA (99.15% uptime), and security (ISO certifications). The customer agreed to receive a quotation and proceed with a pilot, with a decision expected within a week after internal review with directors.","overall_sentiment":{"positive":75,"neutral":20,"negative":5},"key_pain_points":["Current reliance on WhatsApp for internal communication, lacking structured collaboration","Using multiple disjointed apps (Zoom, Gmail, etc.) causing inefficiency and context switching","Manual and paper-based approval processes slowing down operations","Difficulty in managing cross-departmental projects and tracking tasks","Need for a unified platform to reduce tool sprawl and improve employee productivity"],"customer_needs":["Integrated messaging, calendar, video meetings, and document collaboration in one tool","Automated approval workflows to digitize purchasing, leave requests, and other processes","A flexible database (Lark Base) to manage projects, CRM, and custom fields with automation","Real-time translation for multilingual meetings (English, Chinese, Indonesian)","Simple onboarding and training for non-technical users to ensure adoption"],"key_discussions":["Demo of Lark Messenger, Calendar, Meetings with translation, Lark Base, Approval, and Moments","Comparison of Lark Pro vs Enterprise editions: storage, meeting minutes, base rows, workflow limits, security features (watermark, IP restrictions)","Implementation roadmap: Kick-off, admin onboarding, user training, adoption, and quarterly reviews","SLA details: 99.15% uptime, support via official group and Lark support (17\\/7 for chat, 12\\/5 for technical)","Server location: Singapore and Japan, not China, with data security ISO certifications"],"decisions_agreements":["Customer agreed to receive a quotation for 80 Lark Pro users","Next step: Prasetya will send the quotation and a step-by-step timeline for implementation","Customer will share the contact person and decision-maker for the quotation (likely director\\/procurement)","Potential follow-up meeting to address technical questions and finalize pricing"]},"meeting_type_sections":{"features_demonstrated":["Lark Messenger: chat-centric interface with reminders and calendar integration","Lark Calendar: schedule meetings, room booking with approval, and auto-generate meeting links","Lark Meetings: real-time translation (15 languages), screen sharing, and subtitle support","Lark Base: next-level Excel with automation, custom fields, reminders, and email triggers","Lark Approval: digital approval forms for purchasing, leave, etc., with drag-and-drop no-code setup"],"customer_reactions":["High interest in Lark Base, specifically its ability to replace Excel and automate tasks","Positive reaction to real-time translation feature, noting value for multilingual teams","Curiosity about room booking conflicts and approval hierarchy for meeting rooms","Expressed confusion about Lark Base terminology but willing to learn with proper training","Appreciated the structured implementation roadmap and dedicated support from Prasetya"],"questions_objections":["How does room booking handle simultaneou