1	2	1	{"meeting_type":"Discovery","summary_type":"Discovery","general_sections":{"executive_summary":"PT Prasetia Dwidharma is evaluating Lark Suite through a limited pilot, not as an immediate replacement for all existing tools. The main business objective is to make project-related processes more connected, auditable, and efficient across sales, presales, project management, finance, procurement, and implementation teams. The strongest pain points are fragmented information across WhatsApp, email, Google Drive, OneDrive, spreadsheets, and inconsistent task tools; weak sales-to-project handover; manual project reporting; inconsistent approvals; and difficulty finding prior project knowledge. A proposed pilot will focus on sales-to-project handover, project tracking, and potentially resource request approval, with AI meeting summary as a supporting accelerator. Security, API, SSO, integrations, and AI data handling require a separate technical workshop with IT before broader commitment.","key_discussion_points":["Current collaboration is fragmented across WhatsApp, email, Google Drive, OneDrive, spreadsheets, task tools, and manual forms.","Sales-to-project handover is a major pain point due to scattered customer requirements, proposal versions, presales notes, and key decisions remaining in WhatsApp or separate files.","Project tracking is not standardized; some projects follow defined phases while others remain broadly marked as ongoing.","Management visibility into project status, pipeline, risks, delays, and resource load requires manual weekly consolidation.","Internal approvals are inconsistent across email, chat, manual forms, and spreadsheets, with a strong need for conditional routing and audit trail.","Knowledge management is weak because users struggle to find project documents, lessons learned, templates, examples, and technical decisions.","The customer wants a pilot-first approach rather than replacing all tools at once.","AI meeting summary is interesting for summaries, decisions, action items, PICs, due dates, and follow-up, but must be reviewed by users before updating records or creating tasks.","External collaboration is interesting but not part of the first pilot due to permission and security concerns.","Mobile experience is important for approvals, task updates, status checks, photo uploads, and field evidence submission.","Lark should be positioned as an outcome-driven work management and collaboration platform, not merely chat or application consolidation."],"customer_needs_pain_points":["No single source of truth for project information, documents, decisions, and handover context.","Version control issues in proposals, scope of work, project plans, meeting minutes, and UAT documents.","Manual weekly reporting takes approximately one to two hours per project manager depending on project volume.","Meeting minutes take approximately 30 minutes to one hour after each meeting, sometimes more.","Project handover can take several days when information is incomplete.","Approval requests can be delayed or lost because approvers miss messages or requests are spread across channels.","Project managers currently create folders, workspaces, task lists, and kickoff documents manually by copying from prior projects, creating risks around old documents and permissions.","Need flexible but governed project templates for implementation, managed service, integration, and proof of concept projects.","Need dashboards for project health, progress, overdue tasks, blockers, upcoming milestones, risks, resource load, active projects, project value, resource utilization, and customer issues.","Need auditability for approvals, including who approved, when, and comments.","Need role-based and project-based permissions because operations are matrix-based.","Need careful handling of sensitive data such as pricing, margin, contracts, customer data, and technical credentials.","Need adoption-friendly workflows because many users still feel chat is sufficient and will resist systems with too many steps."],"decision_agreement":["PT Prasetia Dwidharma will evaluate Lark Suite through a limited pilot rather than a full tool replacement.","Core proposed pilot areas are sales-to-project handover and project tracking.","Resource request approval is a strong candidate for the pilot but remains subject to validation with the resource manager.","AI meeting summary will be treated as a supporting feature, not a separate pilot workstream.","The first pilot should be internal only, without customer guest access.","Pilot participant estimate is 40 to 60 users, with approximately 20 to 30 core users and the rest as approvers or stakeholders.","Pilot duration under consideration is six to eight weeks.","Security, API, SSO, AI data handling, and integrations will be handled in a separate technical session with IT.","Full offline capability will not be assumed or committed before technical validation.","Email migration, payroll, core finance, secret management, full historical document migration, and full resource capacity planning are out of scope for the pilot."],"action_items":["PT Prasetia Dwidharma: Kodrat Santoso to send sanitized examples of current handover templates and weekly project reports within three working days.","PT Prasetia Dwidharma: Kodrat Santoso to propose business workshop participants, targeted by the end of next week.","PT Prasetia Dwidharma: Kodrat Santoso to identify PICs from IT, including Head of IT and infrastructure representative, for the technical session; exact names not yet available.","Virtuenet: Send a minimum data request list for prototype preparation by tomorrow afternoon.","Virtuenet: Prepare draft use cases and fit-gap analysis.","Virtuenet: Build a simple prototype covering handover, project tracking, approval, and AI meeting summary.","Virtuenet: Propose separate agendas for business workshop and technical workshop.","Virtuenet: Prepare a demo storyline showing end-to-end process from opportunity handover through approval, project creation, tracking, meeting summary, dashboard, and mobile approval\\/task update.","Virtuenet: Send meeting summary on the same day for Kodrat's review, especially scope and assumptions."],"risks_concerns":["No approved budget yet; business case must justify value before procurement and management approval.","Final decision makers were not present in the meeting.","IT and security stakeholders were not present, so requirements for data residency, retention, DLP, SSO, audit log, AI data processing, and integration remain incomplete.","Potential user resistance because some users believe chat and spreadsheets are sufficient.","Pilot may be constrained by user availability due to ongoing large projects.","Data quality and lack of clean initial data may slow the pilot.","Overly broad scope could reduce pilot speed and adoption.","Excessive notifications may cause users to ignore alerts.","External collaboration carries permission risks around internal documents, pricing, and unfinished discussions.","Offline capability for field usage is uncertain and must be technically validated.","Competitors or alternatives include Microsoft 365 and prior project management tools, so Lark must show integrated process value beyond chat and documents."],"next_step":["Virtuenet to send meeting summary and minimum data request list.","PT Prasetia Dwidharma to provide sanitized handover and weekly project report templates.","Virtuenet to prepare draft use cases, fit-gap, and simple prototype after receiving customer templates.","Conduct a business workshop with representatives from sales, presales, project management, resource management, and finance approver.","Conduct a separate technical workshop with IT covering security, API, SSO, integration, AI data handling, and offline validation.","Prepare pilot proposal with scope options for six and eight weeks, success metrics, assumptions, exclusions, and business justification.","If prototype shows value, Kodrat will involve decision makers in a later session."],"missing_information":["Approved budget or budget range is not available.","Final names of decision makers are not available; only roles were discussed.","Final IT PIC names are not available.","Final pilot scope is not confirmed, especially resource request approval.","Detailed procurement process, commercial evaluation criteria, and vendor registration requirements are not fully available.","Data residency, retention, DLP, and detailed security requirements are not available.","Identity provider and internal directory details are not available.","API, webhook, and integration technical requirements are not fully defined.","Offline capability requirements and Lark technical fit are not validated.","Baseline metrics are not finalized; customer prefers measuring baseline during the first two weeks of pilot.","Actual current templates and sanitized sample data are pending.","Final participant list for business workshop is not available.","CRM, ERP, project system, and automation tool details are not available.","Formal company KPI tied to this initiative is not available."]},"meeting_type_sections":{"discovery_objectives":["Understand PT Prasetia Dwidharma's current collaboration and project execution workflows.","Identify operational pain points across sales, presales, implementation, finance, procurement, and project management.","Prioritize use cases suitable for a limited Lark Suite pilot.","Define boundaries, risks, success metrics, and next validation steps for business and technical stakeholders."],"current_state":["Fast communication mostly uses WhatsApp.","Formal communication uses email.","Documents are stored across Google Drive and OneDrive depending on division.","Work tracking is split between spreadsheets and non-standard task management applications.","Approvals happen through email, chat, manual forms, and some forms depending on process.","Project reporting is manually consolidated weekly from multiple files.","Project workspace and kickoff artifacts are manually copied from prior projects, with no automatic provisioning.","Resource availability is tracked in a spreadsheet but not always updated in real time."],"business_challenges":["Fragmented channels cause missing context and inconsistent information flow from opportunity to delivery.","Sales-to-project handover is delayed or incomplete because proposal versions, presales notes, and important decisions are scattered.","Delivery teams may misunderstand scope because sales context and delivery context are not aligned.","Management dashboards require significant manual work behind the scenes.","Approval evidence is hard to retrieve during audit or monthly reviews.","Knowledge depends heavily on individuals; when the information owner is on leave, others struggle to find context.","Adoption of previous tools has been inconsistent due to complexity, excessive configuration, difficult integrations, and users returning to WhatsApp and spreadsheets."],"primary_use_cases_identified":[{"use_case":"Sales-to-project handover","priority":"High","details":["Sales submits structured handover data.","Presales confirms technical scope.","Project manager checks completeness and accepts or returns handover with reasons.","Finance may validate terms or purchase order conditionally for certain projects.","After acceptance, system should create a project workspace or project record from a selected template.","Proposal and scope documents should be referenced as single sources, not copied into multiple uncontrolled versions."]},{"use_case":"Project tracking and workspace","priority":"High","details":["Each project should have milestones, tasks, owners, due dates, status, risks, issues, blockers, and weekly updates.","Dashboards should show overdue tasks, blockers, upcoming milestones, project health, and management-level visibility.","Project templates should support implementation, managed service, integration, and proof of concept categories.","Project health should be based on transparent rules and actual data, with AI only as supporting insight."]},{"use_case":"Resource request approval","priority":"Medium to High, subject to validation","details":["Project manager requests role, skill, number of people, start date, duration, location, allocation, and urgency.","Approval should follow agreed routing.","Availability verification remains manual by resource manager during pilot.","Integration with full capacity planning is deferred to a later phase."]},{"use_case":"AI meeting summary and action items","priority":"Supporting feature","details":["Generate meeting summary, decisions, pain points, action items, PICs, due dates, and recommendations.","User review is required before tasks are created or records are updated.","Meeting summaries should support Indonesian and English templates where possible.","Sensitive customer meeting data should not be used before security review."]}],"pilot_scope":{"proposed_core_scope":["Structured sales-to-project handover","Project workspace and project tracking","Dashboard for project health and management visibility"],"candidate_scope":["Resource request approval, subject to validation with resource manager"],"supporting_capabilities":["AI meeting summary with human review","Mobile approval and mobile task update","Notifications and reminders for overdue tasks and stalled approvals"],"pilot_users":"Estimated 40 to 60 users total, with 20 to 30 core users and remaining users as approvers or stakeholders.","pilot_duration":"Six to eight weeks under consideration.","pilot_mode":"Internal only for the first pilot; no customer guest access initially.","out_of_scope":["Payroll","Core finance replacement","Customer credential management or secret management","Full historical document migration","Full resource capacity planning","Email migration","Replacing ERP or core financial system"]},"success_metrics":["Reduction in time