6	25	1	{"meeting_type":"Demo","summary_type":"Demo","general_sections":{"executive_summary":"Virtuenet conducted a 60-minute Lark Suite demo for PT Prasetia Dwidharma focused on an end-to-end project delivery workflow using Lark Base, Messenger, Calendar, Automation, Task, Dashboard, and related approval concepts. The customer responded positively, especially to Lark Base as a centralized project data hub, Automation for task templates\\/reminders\\/escalations, and Dashboard for operational and management visibility with drill-down. The opportunity shows high interest, but the customer emphasized that any pilot decision remains subject to technical validation, security review, permission\\/governance design, and a clear source-of-truth decision for project tasks.","overall_sentiment":{"positive":75,"neutral":20,"negative":5},"key_pain_points":["Project handover is often incomplete, requiring project managers to manually check documents and scope details.","Project managers want to avoid repeated data entry across task, calendar, and dashboard tools.","Current visibility into overdue tasks and risks is delayed, often only appearing during weekly meetings.","Decisions and issue discussions can be scattered in chat channels and not connected to project records.","The customer is concerned that flexible tools may become difficult to govern without admin controls, permissions, and change management."],"customer_needs":["A centralized project management data model covering handover, project master, tasks, risks\\/issues, resources, and weekly updates.","Automation for handover review, task template generation, reminders, escalation, and weekly update follow-up.","Operational and management dashboards with drill-down, transparent project health rules, data freshness indicators, and permission controls.","Clear security, permission, audit log, user lifecycle, external sharing, retention, backup, recovery, and AI data processing validation.","A limited tailored prototype and hands-on trial before any final pilot recommendation."],"key_discussions":["Demo scenario covered request intake, handover, project provisioning, team coordination, scheduling, approval, task management, escalation, and dashboard monitoring.","Lark Base was positioned as the primary project data hub, with relationships across Project Request, Project Master, Project Task, Risk and Issue, Resource Request, and Weekly Update tables.","The team discussed whether project tasks should live in Lark Task native or Lark Base, agreeing that source of truth must be decided before the pilot.","Formal approvals should use Lark Approval where auditability and approver chains are required, while Base can remain the tracking and orchestration layer.","Security, permission, notification governance, integration design, admin governance, and data freshness were repeatedly raised as prerequisites for scale-up."],"decisions_agreements":["Customer agreed to proceed toward a tailored prototype, subject to security and technical validation.","Proposed pilot scope includes project handover, project provisioning, task template generation, weekly updates, dashboards, and project handover approval.","Full historical migration, ERP integration, company-wide rollout, and full SSO implementation are out of scope for the initial pilot.","Business Design Workshop and Technical\\/Security Workshop will be scheduled as separate sessions.","Pilot decision is not final; opportunity status is high interest with technical validation required and pilot scope under discussion."]},"meeting_type_sections":{"features_demonstrated":["Lark Base for project delivery management data structure, linked records, formulas, views, permissions, and dashboards.","Automation for notifications, task template creation, reminders, escalation, weekly update follow-up, and status updates.","Dashboard for project health, active projects, overdue tasks, risks, completion, filters, and drill-down to actionable records.","Messenger and Calendar for contextual notifications, message cards, project communication, kickoff scheduling, availability, and reminders.","Task management options using Lark Task native versus task tracking in Base, including owners, due dates, status, blockers, and dependencies."],"customer_reactions":["Base received the strongest positive response as a central hub for project data and tracking.","Automation was rated highly for reducing manual work through task templates, reminders, and escalation.","Dashboard was strongly valued, especially for operational drill-down and project health visibility.","Messenger and Calendar were seen as important supporting layers, but with governance concerns around notification overload and source-of-truth design.","ICT considered the platform relevant but required security validation, permission design, auditability, and admin governance before pilot approval."],"questions_objections":["Whether view filters are security controls; clarified that permissions must be configured separately from views.","Whether automation has logs and how failures, external API credentials, and middleware logging should be handled.","Whether Calendar and Base can synchronize two-way; customer preferred a clear source-of-truth approach to avoid conflicts.","Whether Lark Task native and Base task tracking can coexist; customer raised concern about dual task systems confusing users.","Whether business-day SLA calculation, GPS capture, dashboard export, audit log export, backup\\/recovery, and external sharing controls are supported; these remain validation items."],"key_takeaways":["The customer has high interest in Lark Suite for project collaboration and project governance, especially Base, Automation, and Dashboard.","Technical and security validation are mandatory before trial and pilot decision.","Task source of truth is a critical design decision for the pilot.","The customer wants a tailored prototype with real-like process templates rather than 