ff scheduling, availability checks, reminders, and project communication.","Task and approval scenarios covering project task tracking, task dependencies, mobile updates, formal handover approval, and conditional routing."],"customer_reactions":["Base received the strongest positive response as a central project data and tracking layer.","Automation was rated highly because it can reduce manual work through task templates, reminders, escalation, and status orchestration.","Dashboard was strongly valued, especially drill-down from charts into actionable task, risk, and milestone records.","Messenger and Calendar were seen as useful supporting layers but require notification governance and clear source-of-truth decisions.","ICT viewed the platform as relevant but emphasized that security, permission design, auditability, and admin governance must be validated before pilot approval."],"questions_objections":["Whether Base views are security controls; clarified that filters are only display controls and permissions must be used for security.","Whether automation has logs, error handling, and secure credential management for integrations; custom integration should use middleware and secret management.","Whether task management should use native Lark Task or Base; customer objected to having two competing task systems.","Whether Calendar and Base should synchronize two-way; customer preferred a clear source-of-truth approach to avoid conflicts.","Whether dashboard data can include ERP revenue\\/billing and remain fresh; ERP integration was deferred and data freshness indicators were requested."],"key_takeaways":["Meeting outcome was positive and productive, with high interest but no final pilot approval yet.","Highest-interest areas are Lark Base, Automation, and Dashboard.","Primary blockers are technical validation, security validation, source-of-truth design, and governance model definition.","Pilot should remain focused and exclude ERP integration, full historical mig