12	61	1	{"meeting_type":"Demo","summary_type":"Demo","general_sections":{"executive_summary":"Leadsy\\/Lark conducted a broad demo for PT Maju Gemilang Persada covering Lark as an all-in-one collaboration platform for internal communication, meetings, approvals, workflows, Lark Base, dashboards, automation, HR use cases, and potential operational use cases for sales orders, procurement\\/vendor portal, e-commerce reporting, warehouse coordination, and recruitment. The customer showed active interest, especially around replacing fragmented WhatsApp\\/Excel-based processes, maintaining communication history, enabling approvals with audit trails, capturing customer orders through forms before entering Odoo, and using dashboards\\/automation. The discussion also clarified that Odoo remains the ERP\\/process system, while Lark would mainly support collaboration, communication, forms, workflow capture, and potentially integration. Pricing, starter\\/free trial limitations, Pro licensing, frontline licensing, and paid custom use-case development were discussed, but no final purchase decision or confirmed rollout timeline was made.","overall_sentiment":{"positive":70,"neutral":25,"negative":5},"key_pain_points":["Internal communication and work discussions are fragmented across WhatsApp, WeChat, email, Zoom, Excel, and other tools, making history, search, and control difficult.","Customer order intake currently relies heavily on WhatsApp\\/manual handling, creating risk of missing details, duplicate work, and limited structured reporting before data enters Odoo.","Approval processes exist in some systems but several departmental workflows are still conventional\\/verbal\\/WhatsApp-based and need better evidence, notification, and audit trail.","HR processes such as attendance, payroll inputs, leave, overtime, and recruitment are still partly manual or not covered by a complete HRIS.","Warehouse stock opname and item tracking are manual\\/time-consuming; the team mentioned b