24	72	1	{"meeting_type":"Demo","summary_type":"Demo","general_sections":{"executive_summary":"PT Katsushiro Indonesia, a manufacturing company, participated in a demo of Lark (a collaboration tool from ByteDance) presented by Fitrat Adiyuliandito and Kodrat Santoso from Prasetyo, an official Lark partner. The meeting focused on demonstrating Lark's messaging, calendar, video conferencing, AI meeting notes, and workflow approval features. The customer, currently using Microsoft Teams, expressed interest in transitioning to Lark for internal communication and process automation. Key discussions included licensing models (Enterprise vs. A2\\/Frontline), pricing (Rp 350,000 per user per month for Enterprise), storage, security, and integration with existing email systems. The customer showed strong interest in approval workflows and Lark Base, and requested a detailed proposal for 12 Enterprise users with potential expansion to 25 users. Next steps include sending a formal proposal and scheduling training sessions.","overall_sentiment":{"positive":70,"neutral":25,"negative":5},"key_pain_points":["Current Microsoft Teams lacks integrated workflow approval and automation features.","Difficulty in managing meeting room bookings and approvals manually.","Need for a unified collaboration platform that reduces email storage and improves efficiency.","Concerns about data migration and backup for custom applications built in Lark.","Limited budget and need for cost-effective licensing (e.g., considering A2 for managerial level)."],"customer_needs":["A scalable collaboration tool with strong security and storage capabilities.","Integrated approval workflows for purchase requests, travel orders, and other processes.","Ability to create custom applications (e.g., visitor management, meeting room booking) without heavy IT involvement.","AI-powered meeting summaries and live translation for multilingual teams (Japanese, English, Indonesian).","Clear licensing model that allows mixin