ion, partner/channel coordination, meeting management, shared documentation, workflow approvals, and task tracking.	The company may already use established productivity tools such as Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, or internal TP-Link global systems. As a technology company, they may have strict security, compliance, and corporate IT approval requirements. If software procurement is centralized regionally or globally, local decision-making authority may be limited. The absence of recent activity signals reduces visibility into immediate buying intent.
