ntrol issues, limited management visibility, slow approvals, and difficulty finding project knowledge. The strongest pilot candidates are sales-to-project handover, project tracking, and resource request approval, with AI meeting summary as a supporting accelerator subject to review and security validation. The customer is interested in a limited internal pilot of approximately 40-60 users, with 20-30 core users, over 6-8 weeks, but budget is not approved and final decision makers such as Director, Head of IT, Finance, and Procurement are not yet fully engaged.", "action_items": [], "objections_detected": [], "presales_recommendation": "Proceed with a focused, outcome-based prototype and pilot proposal. Do not lead with generic Lark chat or feature breadth; instead demonstrate an end-to-end storyline from opportunity handover to project creation, tracking, approval, AI-assisted meeting summary, dashboard, and mobile actions. Keep scope controlled, validate resource request with the resource manager, separate business and technical workshops, prepare a clear fit-gap, and explicitly address security, AI data processing, permissions, SSO, API, audit log, and offline limitations without overpromising."}	64	{"summary": "Virtuenet conducted a 60-minute end-to-end Lark Suite demo for PT Prasetia Dwidharma focused on project delivery management using Lark Base, Messenger, Calendar, Automation, Task, Dashboard, and handover approval concepts. The customer responded positively, especially to Base as a project data hub, Automation for task creation/reminders/escalation, and Dashboard for operational and management visibility. Interest is high and the team agreed to proceed toward a tailored prototype, but pilot approval is not final and remains dependent on technical/security validation, permission design, task source-of-truth decisions, and governance clarity.", "action_items": [], "objections_detected": [], "presales_recommendation": "Proceed with a tightly scoped prototype 